## 4. Add test fixtures and snapshot for a new rule
Blanks: {rule_id} rule identifier used in expected-error markers; {rule_alias} alias used in markdownlint-configure-file comment; {fixture} fixture file base name; {param} parameter configured in the fixture
1. Create `test/{fixture}.md` fixture(s): a main one that configures the rule via `<!-- markdownlint-configure-file { ... } -->` (disable unrelated rules that would interfere) with `{rule_id}` markers (`{rule_id}:-1` for offset lines) on every line expected to be reported; a `-default` fixture showing no reports with default config; extra fixtures for variants (e.g. setext headings).
2. In test/markdownlint-test.mjs, add a dedicated test at the end of the suite (with t.plan) covering the rule's special branches, such as invalid parameter values. (only if the rule has a branch not covered by fixtures, since the repo requires full coverage)

