   `test/markdownlint-test-project.mjs:37-60` in test.suite(import.meta.url.replace(/^.*?\/(?<name>[^/]*)$/u, "$<nam... › test("projectFilesExtendedAscii", (t) => {
   ```
      37|   test("projectFilesExtendedAscii", (t) => {
        ⋮
      54|       const expected = {};
      55|       for (const file of filteredFiles) {
      56|         expected[file] = [];
      57|       }
      58|       t.assert.deepEqual(actual, expected, "Issue(s) with project files.");
      59|     });
      60|   });
   ```
3. In test/markdownlint-test.mjs, increase t.plan in the "readme" test (more rule row/tag assertions per new rule).
4. In test/markdownlint-test.mjs, increase t.plan in the "validateJsonUsingConfigSchemaStrict" test.
5. In test/markdownlint-test.mjs, increase t.plan in the "allBuiltInRulesHaveValidUrl" test (one per new rule plus extra assertions).
6. In test/markdownlint-test.mjs, increase t.plan in the "version numbers match" test.
7. Run `npm test` and adjust each plan count to the 'plan expected' numbers reported until it passes.

